DESCRIPTION >
    Reporting categories by requesting account: regular, legacy, operations
    (pollinationsagent: bots, monitors, automation) and dev (staff accounts).
    user_id is the key owner, so staff testing through an app counts as dev.
    Legacy is matched by its two bridge keys first because they live on the
    pollinationsagent account. Update the dev accounts when the team changes.
    Changing these rules requires repopulating the dependent usage, BYOP and
    first-activity aggregates.

NODE classified_events
SQL >
    SELECT
        *,
        multiIf(
            api_key_id IN (
                'lIa3Q9Wdq2jAw1mkdI38g5zpsaZr45qz', -- raw-buzzard: legacy image
                '89idjaTSg2hI4YwZDuO8ZME5Ma6GrFps' -- legacy text
            ), 'legacy',
            user_id = 'LJVtOPiUl0C4uRku8kL8prpp95m8jLnt', 'operations', -- pollinationsagent
            user_id IN (
                '328eJMEXiBAhRskZcmKINOx3CoidBc6x', -- ElliotEtag
                'ds1EIz1ELXSNZzzRKJ0jrCsGgLeiVfRh', -- elliot@pollinations.ai
                'pSuZFfxdFpRIDq0MJKwvT1y4LZ7cyA9n', -- voodoohop (Thomas)
                'oUHeC9bMreSyrFhF9OYwF0vIJvkBugw3' -- thomashmyceli (Thomas)
            ), 'dev',
            'regular'
        ) AS traffic_group
    FROM generation_event_v2
